C|DO NOT RUN git commit AND DO NOT RUN pairctl. Your sandbox on this machine denies git's index.lock even with --add-dir, and three rounds have already been lost to retrying it. Make the changes, run the two verification commands, leave the work uncommitted in the worktree, and report what you changed in your final message. The auditor commits.
C|Do not add any using-alias directive. FKNRTD.Services is already imported where it is needed.
A|FIX A - ordering: LogFormat.Read answers type 'system' BEFORE it checks for failure, so {"type":"system","is_error":true,"message":"Authentication failed"} reads as 'session started' noise. Move the system branch after the failure detection so a failing system record reads as LogKind.Failed carrying its message. A system record with no failure signal must still read as noise exactly as today.
A|FIX B - case: LogFormat's property lookups (Text, Flag, Detail) use JsonElement.TryGetProperty, which is case-sensitive, so IS_ERROR is ignored. AgentOutputObserver.FindString matches property names with OrdinalIgnoreCase. Make LogFormat match the observer: a record carrying IS_ERROR true must read as a failure.
A|FIX C - first block wins: LogFormat.FromContent returns on the first recognised block, so a content array whose first block is text and whose second is a tool_result with is_error true reports only the text and loses the failure. Scan every block; a failed tool_result anywhere in the array must win over an earlier text or tool_use block. With no failed block present, behaviour is unchanged - the first recognised block still wins.
A|FIX D - lost exit status: LogFormat.FromItem renders a command_execution as '> ' + command and drops the command's exit status and output entirely, so a failed build reads identically to a successful one. Carry the exit status: a command that exited non-zero must read as LogKind.Failed and say so. VERIFY the actual field names Codex emits rather than assuming - check tests/FKNRTD.SelfTest/Program.cs:3638 and AgentOutputObserver for what this codebase already believes, tolerate the fields being absent, and state in your report which field names you relied on and what evidence you had for them.
